Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraScene", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"b92c4df0-2e50-49a1-a32b-5c5fa1439d66"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraScene"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraScene", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     StyleBox["objects", "TI"], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     StyleBox["steps", "TI"], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f56d489-3c8b-4f61-90ff-4f8ff3afddb5"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is a construction: a list of object names, and a list of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraGeometricStep"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeometricStep", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ddd8779f-1458-428d-a60f-7ff32a20354e"],
 " constraints that define them.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d63c84c8-8d24-4f58-8600-346f9ac0f2bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a scene names some objects and states constraints relating \
them. It is a construction written down, not yet carried out. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e6552c9c-8d01-456f-a368-0855d1e17ef5"],
 " carries it out."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f19ccd19-d10b-42fc-becb-08115e24b8f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is how a ruler-and-compass construction is expressed. Each step is a \
constraint of the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"object", " ", "==", " ", 
   RowBox[{"constructor", "[", "...", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cdb3f27d-8f16-43be-99e6-c26a21c9f62d"],
 ", optionally with side conditions like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"u", " ", "!=", " ", "v"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8f0a1b3-ca6d-417b-92d5-b03bbda57266"],
 ". Later steps may refer to objects bound by earlier ones, so the steps read \
in the order Euclid writes them."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f523cdae-9890-4cca-9ba8-fc160ebe9399"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inside a scene the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Infra", "*"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9fd8e3a-1e7f-4680-961a-ad3318706f82"],
 " heads are ",
 StyleBox["constructors",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", not values. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraPoint", "[", "v", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02e0a91d-fa0d-4e65-960e-a38f7ea3c75d"],
 " names a point at ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraSegment", "[", 
   RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "q"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50e80a3c-e27a-4b9d-8463-0ab78228f900"],
 " names the segment between two named points. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraCircle", "[", 
   RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "816c0fc2-59df-43d5-8cde-6fbccf82f638"],
 " names a circle of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] inside a scene the token still reads ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " as a radius, unlike the head, where a bare second argument is always a \
point; this is an open inconsistency. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraIntersection", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba110dfb-138a-4660-ba78-91f4962e4345"],
 " names where two named objects meet. The names are ordinary symbols, so \
they must be undefined when the scene is built \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData["ClearAll"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a599914-7b08-41cb-a6a1-2647b8a61b5f"],
 " them first."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ddfdad65-c579-43cb-b246-fc09e60da4cb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The whole of Euclidean construction is available: circles and their \
intersections are what a compass is for, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3a5e0c98-1564-4907-af3e-f7b77098a8fa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraIntersection"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraIntersection", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "bb1bdd25-bdde-41ac-9c56-c3b96e47b091"],
 " carry most of the work. Use circles, not level sets \[LongDash] a circle \
is the geometric object, and a shell is the set it was cut from."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7987d85d-fd2b-4e72-977f-5166bd658977"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Accessors: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Objects\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "88fd0d61-a028-4dc2-9384-490a04927572"],
 " the names, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Labels\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63d42ab0-7641-4bee-878c-0f8c35a04d05"],
 " the step labels, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Constructions\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "270d349b-3658-4588-8e20-8ebbfc495e6f"],
 " the constraint for each object, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Steps\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e7e71b22-8086-48f3-bfd1-b5a56de67f43"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Assertions\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ccb12166-a92d-4af3-a7a5-25c0e8f7d6e8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<DependencyGraph\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70642113-d820-47a4-adf3-a3a93d9dee70"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e4950ad8-6603-4e1d-9f43-d53d96f4691a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two practical notes. Solving is done step by step, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FindInfraScene", "[", 
   RowBox[{"scene", ",", " ", "g", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b0dc909-12d8-4bf6-a7da-f7b2c7efa5db"],
 " solves the first ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " steps, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["k"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a9316d31-8c0a-4e70-a702-ac6788060eca"],
 " is a step index and not a count of solutions. And each step multiplies the \
branching: a step whose object has several admissible realisations produces \
one instance per combination, so the instance count grows as the construction \
proceeds."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6f117218-0d50-4c98-8909-8a7a5690b8bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A construction can stall.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Euclid never postulated that the two circles of I.1 actually meet, and on \
a graph they need not. The same construction that succeeds on a triangulated \
mesh has no solution on a square grid, because there a single distance shell \
spans no cycle, so the circles do not exist. That is the continuity \
assumption Euclid left unstated, showing up as an empty result."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0c9970b3-77b9-4198-ae1a-c53416734cf2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Bind every construction to a name.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " An operand of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraIntersection"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraIntersection", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a6bbbce5-398d-4340-8447-b8a79e668cc8"],
 " must be a name bound by an earlier step, not an inline constructor. \
Writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraIntersection", "[", 
   RowBox[{"cA", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"InfraCircle", "[", 
     RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5514e5a0-6c1d-4d48-8e44-ac2c386d9d97"],
 " fails, because the inline constructor is never dispatched and reaches the \
set operation with its own head intact. Give the circle its own step and \
refer to it by name, as below."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"34c3b6f2-ec2a-4079-ad26-9737968d5672"]
}, Open  ]],

